upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about the historical development of communications (as distinct from transport), per Goh Cheng Leong:\n1. Communication refers to the transmission of messages, distinct from the physical carriage of goods and people.\n2. The invention of writing was a milestone allowing messages to be permanently recorded and transmitted over unlimited distances.\n3. Telecommunications (telegraph, telephone, radio, television, satellites) represent an earlier stage of communication development than the establishment of postal systems.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1 and 2 only","1 and 3 only","2 and 3 only","1, 2 and 3"],"a":0,"e":"Statement 3 is incorrect and reverses the chronological sequence — the text describes the sequence as: oral communication, then writing, then postal systems, and only later telecommunications (telegraph/telephone/radio/TV/satellites) as the 'climax' of this development, not an earlier stage. Statements 1 and 2 are correct."})

